course: dictionary
lesson: 2053
title: Conscience: the inner voice
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Your conscience is the inner voice that tells you what is right and what is wrong. «A guilty conscience, like not sleeping or not looking someone in the eye, is a sign that something needs putting right.» So when you do wrong, your conscience makes you feel bad inside.
explain: A «clear conscience» is the opposite. It means you have done nothing wrong, so you feel calm about it. «Conscience is the inner sense of right and wrong; guilt is the bad feeling after doing something wrong.» Guilt is what you feel, and conscience is the sense that tells you it is there.
explain: Read the words around conscience to find its meaning. In «a quiet kindness nobody knows about can feel lovely, while cheating unseen often leaves a weird feeling», the clue is the weird feeling after cheating. Try putting "inner voice" in place of conscience and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Conscience means your inner sense of right and wrong.
fact: Many Christians believe the conscience helps us know God's law, and they examine their conscience before confession.
fact: «Guilty conscience» and «clear conscience» are opposites: one makes you feel bad, the other makes you feel calm.
fact: Conscience is spelled C-O-N-S-C-I-E-N-C-E, "con" + "science", from Latin.
fact: «In all conscience» is a formal phrase meaning honestly and fairly.
exercise: «A guilty conscience, like not sleeping or not looking someone in the eye, is a sign that something needs putting right.» What does a guilty conscience make you feel? | Happy and proud | Very hungry | Calm and sure you did nothing wrong | *Bad inside, because you have done something wrong
exercise: Which phrase means you have done nothing wrong and feel calm? | *A clear conscience | A guilty conscience | Conscience-stricken | A prick of conscience
exercise: «In all conscience» is a formal phrase. What does it mean? | *Honestly, fairly | Very loudly | Quickly and rudely | Inside a cupboard
test: What is your conscience? | A shoe you wear to school | *The inner voice that tells you what is right and wrong | A loud noise in your ear | A type of cloud
test: Which word means the bad feeling after doing something wrong? | Clear | Conscience | Stricken | *Guilt
exam: «Guilt is the conscience working; it is a sign you know what is right, not proof you are a bad person.» What does this sentence tell you? | *Feeling guilty shows you know what is right, but it does not make you a bad person | Guilt is the same as a clear conscience | Guilt means you are hungry | Guilt proves you are a bad person
